# Architecture — custom store

## Context

The project uses a tiny in-house store (`app/src/store.ts`) and a discriminated
`Action` union in `app/src/types.ts`. New behaviors must be added via the
Action union and handled in `app/src/reducer.ts`. This preserves the intended
architecture and keeps the store engine untouched.

## Rule

- Do not replace the custom store with Redux, Zustand, MobX, or other state
  libraries.
- To add behavior: extend `Action` in `app/src/types.ts`, handle it in
  `app/src/reducer.ts` (immutably), and expose an action creator in
  `app/src/actions.ts`.
- Add a colocated test that exercises the new action.

## How to verify

1. Confirm no imports of `redux`, `zustand`, `mobx`, or similar in `app/`.
2. New features appear as an Action variant in `app/src/types.ts` and a
   corresponding case in `app/src/reducer.ts`.
3. `app/src/store.ts` remains unchanged (unless explicit approval is given).